
# 🐱🐶 SVM Cat vs Dog Classifier

A fun machine learning project teaching an SVM to distinguish cats from dogs with over 85% accuracy!

## 🎯 Project Overview

- **Images**: 5,000 cats + 5,000 dogs
- **Preprocessing**: Resize to 128×128 pixels, normalize pixel values
- **Model**: Support Vector Machine (SVM)
- **Accuracy**: >85%

## 📁 Project Structure

```
cat-dog-svm/
├── data/                       # 10K resized images
│   ├── cats/
│   └── dogs/
├── train_svm.py               # Training script
├── predict.py                 # Prediction script
├── preprocess.py              # Image preprocessing utilities
└── README.md                  # Project documentation
```

## 🚀 Quick Start

```bash
# Clone and setup
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/cat-dog-svm.git
cd cat-dog-svm

# Install dependencies
pip install numpy scikit-learn opencv-python

# Train the model
python train_svm.py

# Predict on a new image
python predict.py --image path/to/image.jpg
```

## 🤖 SVM Applications

- 🖼️ **Image Classification** (pets, objects)
- 🏥 **Medical Diagnostics** (tumor detection)
- 📝 **Text Classification** (spam filtering)
- 💰 **Finance** (fraud detection)
- 🗣️ **Speech Recognition** (voice commands)

## 📈 Performance Metrics

| Metric    | Score |
|-----------|-------|
| **Precision** | High (few false positives) |
| **Recall**    | High (few false negatives) |
| **F1-Score**  | Balanced performance |

## 💻 Usage Example

```bash
python predict.py --image "data/cats/cat123.jpg"
# Output: Predicted class: Cat, Confidence: 0.92
```

## ⚠️ Disclaimer

This model is for demonstration purposes. Real-world applications require further tuning and validation.
